[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Wanted: a Large Biscuit Tin]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.46]Lesson 26 | 第26课
[00:02.45]Wanted: a large biscuit tin | 征集大饼干筒
[00:11.15]Who won the prize for the biggest biscuit? | 谁赢得了最大饼干的奖品？
[00:15.29]No one can avoid being influenced by advertisements. | 没有人能不受广告的影响。
[00:19.62]Much as we may pride ourselves on our good taste, | 尽管我们可以自夸品味高雅，
[00:23.32]we are no longer free to choose the things we want, | 但我们再也无法随心所欲地挑选自己所需的东西了，
[00:26.61]for advertising exerts a subtle influence on us. | 因为广告在我们身上施加着潜移默化的影响。
[00:30.96]In their efforts to persuade us to buy this or that product, | 在做广告极力劝说我们买这买那的努力中，
[00:35.11]advertisers have made a close study of human nature and have classified all our little weaknesses. | 广告商对人性作了深入研究，并把我们的种种小弱点一一归类。
[00:43.15]Advertisers discovered years ago that all of us love to get something for nothing. | 广告商多年前就发现，我们大家都喜欢白得东西。
[00:48.96]An advertisement which begins with the magic word FREE can rarely go wrong. | 以“免费”这个神奇的词开头的广告很少会失败。
[00:55.87]These days, advertisers not only offer free samples, | 如今，广告商不仅提供免费样品，
[00:59.82]but free cars, free houses, and free trips round the world as well. | 而且还提供免费汽车、免费住房，甚至免费环球旅行。
[01:06.80]They devise hundreds of competitions which will enable us to win huge sums of money. | 他们设计了数百种竞赛，让我们可以赢得大笔的钱。
[01:12.73]Radio and television have made it possible for advertisers to capture the attention of millions of people in this way. | 电台、电视使广告商有可能用这种方式吸引千百万人的注意力。
[01:21.12]During a radio programme, a company of biscuit manufacturers once asked listeners to bake biscuits and send them to their factory. | 在一次电台节目中，一家饼干制造商曾请听众烘烤饼干并送到他们厂里去。
[01:31.29]They offered to pay $10 a pound for the biggest biscuit baked by a listener. | 他们愿意为听众所烤的最大饼干支付每磅10美元的报酬。
[01:37.09]The response to this competition was tremendous. | 这次竞赛的反应极其热烈。
[01:40.86]Before long, biscuits of all shapes and sizes began arriving at the factory. | 不久，形状大小各异的饼干开始源源不断地运到工厂。
[01:47.05]One lady brought biscuit on a wheelbarrow. It weighed nearly 500 pounds. | 一位女士用手推车送来了一个饼干，重达近500磅。
[01:53.41]A little later, a man came along with a biscuit which occupied the whole boot of his car. | 过了一会儿，一个男人也带来了一个饼干，那个饼干把他的整个行李箱都占满了。
[02:00.71]All the biscuits that were sent were carefully weighed. | 所有送来的饼干都仔细地过秤。
[02:04.30]The largest was 713 pounds. It seemed certain that this would win the prize. | 最大的一个重713磅，看来这个饼干稳获头奖了。
[02:12.33]But just before the competition closed, | 但就在竞赛即将结束时，
[02:15.63]a lorry arrived at the factory with a truly colossal biscuit which weighed 2, 400 pounds. | 一辆卡车开到工厂，运来了一个真正巨大的饼干，重达2400磅。
[02:24.44]It had been baked by a college student who had used over 1, 000 pounds of flour, 800 pounds of sugar, | 它是由一名大学生烤制的，用了1000多磅面粉、800磅食糖、
[02:32.59]200 pounds of fat, and 400 pounds of various other ingredients. | 200磅动物脂肪和400磅其他各种原料。
[02:38.26]It was so heavy that a crane had to be used to remove it from the lorry. | 饼干太重了，得用起重机才把它从卡车上卸下来。
[02:43.97]The manufacturers had to pay more money than they had anticipated, for they bought the biscuit from the student for $24, 000. | 制造商付出的钱远远超出了他们的预料，因为他们花2.4万美元从那个大学生手里买下了这块饼干。
